course: dictionary
lesson: 3507
title: Faster: more speed, less time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Faster is the comparing form of fast. Fast means quick, and faster means more quick when you compare two things. «The cheetah runs faster than the rabbit.» Use faster when you are comparing speeds, or when something is happening more quickly.
explain: Faster can also be about time. «Ella finished her sums faster than Sam.» Ella did not run faster. She took less time to finish. So faster can mean moving more quickly, or taking less time to do something.
explain: Faster appears in maths, science and PE. In maths, a faster speed is a slower speed plus a difference. In science, a ball rolls faster down a steeper slope. In PE, you might ask who can run faster. Clues to watch for are phrases like faster and faster, go faster and the faster, the better.
fact: Faster is an adjective and an adverb: fast, faster, fastest.
fact: «Faster» means with more speed, moving or working more quickly.
fact: «Faster» also means taking less time to do something.
fact: A clock that is faster shows a later time than the real time.
fact: «Faster and faster» means the speed keeps going up, as in «say /k/ /a/ /t/ faster and faster and it becomes «cat»».
exercise: «Say /k/ /a/ /t/ faster and faster and it becomes «cat».» What does faster mean here? | Backwards | Louder | *More quickly | Slower and slower
exercise: Ella ran the race in 40 seconds and Sam ran it in 45 seconds. Who was faster? | Neither of them ran | Both were exactly the same | *Ella | Sam
exercise: A clock that is faster shows what? | No time at all | *A later time than the real time | An earlier time than the real time | The same time as the real time
test: In science, a ball rolls faster down a steeper slope. Why does it roll faster? | *Because the slope is steeper | Because the slope is flat | Because it is raining | Because it is lighter
test: Which phrase means the speed keeps getting bigger? | Slower and slower | Stop and start | Once in a while | *Faster and faster
exam: Which sentence uses faster to mean taking less time? | «The river runs faster after the rain.» | «The cheetah is faster than the tortoise.» | *«Ben finished his homework faster than usual.» | «The rabbit hopped faster across the field.»
